prompt:
You are a sceptical financial analyst reviewing a forecast prepared by a colleague.

Given the following forecast for HUDCO (base year 2021):
{
  "strategy": "baseline",
  "base_year": 2021,
  "forecast": [
    {
      "year": 2022,
      "revenue_cr": 7010.43,
      "net_income_cr": 1520.28,
      "eps": 7.59
    },
    {
      "year": 2023,
      "revenue_cr": 6753.18,
      "net_income_cr": 1464.43,
      "eps": 7.31
    },
    {
      "year": 2024,
      "revenue_cr": 6505.44,
      "net_income_cr": 1410.66,
      "eps": 7.04
    }
  ],
  "reasoning": "From the standalone P&L, Total Income (Revenue from Operations + Other Income) was \u20b97,571.64 crore in FY2020 and \u20b97,277.73 crore in FY2021, a YoY decline of approximately -3.88%. Net Income (PAT) was \u20b91,708.42 crore in FY2020 and \u20b91,578.58 crore in FY2021, a YoY decline of approximately -7.60%. Applying these FY2021 growth rates (-3.88% for revenue and -7.60% for net income) as the primary projection assumption for FY2022-2024, with EPS calculated using shares outstanding of 200.19 crore (equity share capital of \u20b92,001.90 crore at face value of \u20b910 per share, consistent with reported Basic EPS of \u20b97.89 for FY2021: 1578.58/200.19 \u2248 7.89)."
}

Step 1: Identify the 3 most critical assumptions embedded in this forecast.
Step 2: For each assumption, describe one plausible scenario where it fails.
Step 3: Rate each assumption failure as Low / Medium / High risk to the forecast accuracy.
Step 4: Assign an overall confidence score from 0-100 (100 = completely certain).

RESPONSE FORMAT: Begin your response DIRECTLY with the opening brace { — no reasoning or text before the JSON.

Return ONLY valid JSON:
{
  "company": "<COMPANY>",
  "base_year": <YYYY>,
  "strategy": "<baseline|alt_strategy>",
  "assumptions": [
    {"assumption": "<text>", "failure_scenario": "<text>", "risk": "<Low|Medium|High>"}
  ],
  "confidence_score": <0-100>,
  "overall_critique": "<2 sentences>"
}

response:
